d 'KMPLOT': module to draw Kaplan-Meier survival, cumulative failure and competing-risks cumulative incidence curves with risk tables
d
d  kmplot draws publication-ready Kaplan-Meier survival and
d cumulative failure curves from stset data, and Aalen-Johansen
d cumulative incidence curves when a competing event is given with
d compete(). Curves can be stratified with by(), drawn with
d log-log, log or plain confidence intervals as bands or lines, and
d annotated with median survival lines, censoring marks and a
d log-rank p-value. An optional number-at-risk table below the plot
d counts people or sums the stset weight, can show cumulative
d events, and can mask small cells for disclosure control. Options
d cover percent scale, truncation of the plot at tmax(), fixed-time
d (landmark) estimates, custom titles, colors and line patterns,
d and export of the graph, the plotted curve data and the
d risk-table counts. The default palette is Okabe-Ito, chosen for
d readers with color-vision deficiency. Medians, landmark estimates
d with confidence limits, the risk-table counts and the log-rank
d p-value are returned in r(). 
d
d KW: Kaplan-Meier
d KW: survival curves
d KW: cumulative failure
d KW: cumulative incidence
d KW: Aalen-Johansen
d KW: competing risks
d KW: number at risk
d KW: risk table
d KW: log-rank test
d KW: graphics
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
f kmplot.ado
f kmplot.sthlp
f ../_/_kmplot_risktable.ado
f ../_/_kmplot_times.ado
f ../_/_kmplot_cif.ado
